PUBLIC RESPONSE: {C}

The ESA requires that any employer with 25+ employees on January 1 of a given year must maintain written policies on disconnecting from work and electronic monitoring. If a policy is created or revised, a copy must be given to every employee within 30 days.  

Option C meets the 25-employee threshold but updates its policies monthly while distributing copies only quarterly. Because a quarterly distribution cycle necessarily exceeds the 30-day statutory window, C is out of compliance as of 2 January 2023.  

All other options either fall below the 25-employee threshold on the relevant January 1 date (so no policy obligation exists) or satisfy both the existence and timely-distribution requirements.}

